        ("What is the difference between synchronous and asynchronous methods in Node.js core modules?", "Synchronous methods (e.g. fs.readFileSync) block the entire Node.js main thread until finished. Asynchronous methods (e.g. fs.readFile) execute non-blockingly via callbacks or promises.", "Easy", "Comparison", "fs.readFileSync('file.txt'); // Blocks\nfs.readFile('file.txt', cb); // Non-blocking", "Why should Sync methods be avoided in servers?"),
